## New laptop setup checklist
1. Install Node.js — nodejs.org
2. Install Homebrew — /bin/bash -c "$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)"
3. Install GitHub CLI — brew install gh
4. Authenticate — gh auth login
5. Clone repo — git clone https://github.com/kulvirpawar92/proflet
6. cd proflet && npm install
7. Create .env file with 3 keys (see .env section below)
8. npm run dev → open http://localhost:5173

## .env file contents (needed on new laptop)
```
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://wjjqgzyjubvhxivlqnxq.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your anon key from Supabase → Settings → API>
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=<your publishable key from Stripe → Developers → API keys>
```
Keep these values saved securely (password manager). The anon key and publishable key are safe to store — they are public-facing keys.

